# Build settings of the plugin. Later sources win: this file, then plugin.local.env (git-ignored,
# for private values such as your domain), then environment variables of the same name.
#   make claude                     -> plugin "swe", entry command /swe, skills /swe:<skill>
#   PLUGIN_NAME=acme make claude    -> plugin "acme", entry command /acme
# Keep values on their own line: no trailing comments.
PLUGIN_NAME ?= swe
PLUGIN_OWNER ?= swe
PLUGIN_VERSION ?= 1.0.0
# Hosts in templates and examples are <service>.<env>.<PLUGIN_DOMAIN>.
PLUGIN_DOMAIN ?= example.com
# PLUGIN_TITLE defaults to PLUGIN_NAME capitalised; PLUGIN_HOMEPAGE to https://<domain>/<name>.
PLUGIN_DESCRIPTION ?= Software engineering skills: one entry command routes every task to a playbook, the principles, and tested skills for Go/Fiber APIs, Python ML, Rust performance code and Next.js / Vite + React frontends, with Postgres, Redis, Kafka, S3, deployment and observability, and does not finish until the service's verify command passes.
